---
import Icon from "../Icon.astro";
import Shot from "../Shot.astro";
import importScreen from "../../assets/screenshots/logistics-import.png";
import importPhone from "../../assets/screenshots/logistics-import-phone.png";
---

<section class="band">
  <div class="page grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10">
    <div class="lg:col-span-6">
      <span class="tile"><Icon name="paperclip" /></span>
      <h2 class="title mt-6">
        Attach it once, access it anywhere.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <p class="lede lg:col-span-6">
      Attach the tickets and hotel confirmations to their booking: everyone on it downloads them from the Personal app. No email attachments, no shared drives, no "which version is the latest?"
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- The other way round: the document creates the booking. Shown at the preview, before anything is saved. -->
  <div class="page mt-16 grid items-start gap-8 md:mt-20 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10">
    <div class="ruled lg:col-span-4">
      <p class="font-display text-lg font-medium text-graphite">Import</p>
      <h3 class="subtitle mt-2 md:text-3xl">Drop the confirmation. Check it. It's filled in.</h3>
      <p class="muted mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Drop the agency's mail or the hotel's PDF on the event: the hotel, the flights, the car or the transfer it holds come out as bookings, with the people named on them. Nothing is saved until you have checked them.
      </p>
      <p class="muted mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        PDF, Excel, CSV, a picture or a screenshot, a mail file (.eml) with its attachments, .ics, HTML or text — up to 10 MB and 30 pages. It creates new bookings; it does not change the ones you already have.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-8">
      <Shot desktop={importScreen} phone={importPhone} alt="RaceNode Logistics import: a travel agency's confirmation on the left, the hotel and flights it holds on the right, to check before importing" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
